# netsurf: frames carried over when a flex or grid container is restyled alone (patch 428)
# Generated 2026-11-09
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 427)
#
# "structural selectors or counters in page CSS" was r140's second
# decline (11); rte gave 5 of them, and 6 "restyled flex or grid box holds
# controls or frames". Logged in a scratch build: rte's carousel (a flex
# container patch 372 restyles alone on each slide) holds its video
# frame -- an <iframe> box (IFRAME, window linked) -- and no local rebuild
# frees a frame's box (patch 371: c->iframe's record and the window point
# at it), so every slide took the full rebuild.
#
# A frame is carried over now (html_rl_frames_carry): box construction
# gives the rebuilt <iframe> box a record of its own (box_iframe prepends
# it to c->iframe); the records made since the build began are the new
# tree's. Each old frame box's window goes to the new box of its element
# (or to none: display:none now) through browser_window_iframe_rebox
# (desktop/frames.c, new: html.c cannot see struct browser_window), and
# the old box's records leave the list and are freed (talloc; a window
# holds the record's values, not the record). The full layout that
# follows places the window (layout.c, by box->iframe); fixes905's
# re-link by element still runs on every reformat. A build that is given
# up drops the records it made (html_rl_frames_drop_new). A frame on the
# container's own box, and selects / file / image inputs, still decline.
# html_rl_subtree_stateful (frames + controls) is now
# html_rl_subtree_controls.
#
# rte (scratch, 2 loads): full rebuilds 8 -> 5, "holds controls or
# frames" 6 -> 0, the structural decline 5 -> 0; 5 frames handed over a
# load.
#
